# The Dockerfile's build stage COPYs exactly three things: Cargo.toml,
# Cargo.lock, and crates/. Everything below is excluded from the build
# context so the daemon never has to read or hash it, whether or not the
# Dockerfile happens to reference it today.
#
# The single biggest win is target/: a full local build tree runs into the
# tens of gigabytes, and it's entirely regenerated by the build stage anyway
# -- shipping it to the daemon would dwarf every other exclusion combined.
# The frontend workspaces (bridge/, sdks/, landing/, examples/,
# study-guide/, cargo-mentor/) add up to roughly another two gigabytes
# across their node_modules trees, none of which the API-only image (see the
# Dockerfile's top comment) ever touches.

# Rust build output. By far the largest thing in the tree; matches at any
# depth so a crate-local target/ (if one is ever created) is caught too.
target/
**/target/

# VCS metadata. Not needed to compile, and salvor-server's build.rs already
# degrades gracefully (omits its optional commit stamp) when no .git is
# present, so excluding it changes nothing user-visible.
.git/
.gitignore

# Frontend workspaces and every node_modules tree: irrelevant to the
# API-only build (see the Dockerfile's top comment for why the UI build
# chain doesn't run here at all).
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
bridge/
sdks/
landing/
examples/
demo/
study-guide/
cargo-mentor/
.internal/
.rdm/

# Docs (screenshots, a demo gif) and repo-root scratch files: not read by
# the build, no reason to upload them to the daemon.
docs/
*.log
*.db
findings.txt
.DS_Store

# Editor/CI config not read during the image build.
.github/
.claude/
